---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../data/legal";
import { links } from "../data/site";
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms for using honeybearkatherine.org: what you may do with the content, what we promise, and what we do not."
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
  current="terms"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to <strong>honeybearkatherine.org</strong>, operated by
    Katherine L. Carter ("we", "us"). By using the site you agree to them. If
    you do not, please do not use it.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>

  <p>
    You may read, share and link to anything here. We encourage it. In return,
    please do not:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Republish articles in full elsewhere without permission. A quotation with a link back is welcome.</li>
    <li>Present our writing as your own, or use it to train a commercial model without asking.</li>
    <li>Attempt to disrupt the site, probe it for vulnerabilities, or access anything not intended to be public.</li>
    <li>Use the site to harass anybody, or to break the law.</li>
    <li>Scrape it in a way that degrades it for other people.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    If you would like to reproduce something — for a class, a support group, a
    newsletter — <a href="/contact">ask us</a>. The answer is usually yes.
  </p>

  <h2>Who owns what</h2>

  <p>
    Articles, episode descriptions, page copy, the HBK777 mark and the site
    design belong to Katherine L. Carter or are used with permission. Episodes
    are published on YouTube and remain subject to YouTube's terms.
  </p>

  <p>
    Quoting a passage with attribution and a link is fair and welcome.
    Reproducing an entire article is not.
  </p>

  <h2>Anything you send us</h2>

  <p>
    If you send a question, a story or a suggestion — by email, through the
    contact form, or in a live show — you keep ownership of it. You give us
    permission to read it, reply to it, and where it is relevant, to discuss the
    substance of it on air or in writing.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>We will not identify you</strong> without your clear permission.
    Stories shared publicly are described in general terms with identifying
    details removed. If you would prefer we do not mention your situation at
    all, say so and we will not.
  </p>

  <h2>Live shows and community spaces</h2>

  <p>
    The show is broadcast in Meta Horizon Worlds and Clubroom, which are run by
    their own companies under their own rules. We do not control those platforms
    and cannot resolve problems that happen on them — use their reporting and
    blocking tools, which are linked from the{" "}
    <a href="/resources">resources page</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    In our rooms, the expectation is simple: people are here about difficult
    personal subjects, so treat them decently. Harassment, abuse and recording
    people without consent will get you removed.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>

  <p>
    The site is provided <strong>as is</strong>. We do not guarantee that it
    will always be available, that it will be free of errors, or that anything
    on it fits your particular circumstances. We may change, move or remove
    content at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, Katherine L. Carter is not liable
    for any indirect, incidental, consequential or special loss arising out of
    your use of this site or reliance on anything published here — including
    decisions you make about a relationship.
  </p>

  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability for anything that cannot lawfully be
    limited, including fraud or personal injury caused by negligence. Some
    jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions, so parts of this section may
    not apply to you.
  </p>

  <p>
    Please read the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> as well. It sets out
    clearly that this site is not therapy, not medical or legal advice, and not
    a crisis service.
  </p>

  <h2>Other people's sites</h2>

  <p>
    We link to organisations, platforms and shops. Those links are for
    convenience and are not an endorsement of everything on the far side of
    them. We do not control that content and are not responsible for it. Some
    links earn a commission, and which ones is set out in the{" "}
    <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Copyright complaints</h2>

  <p>
    If you believe something here infringes your copyright, email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a> with: what the work is,
    where it appears on this site, your contact details, a statement that you
    believe the use is unauthorised, and a statement that your notice is
    accurate and that you are the rights holder or authorised to act for them.
  </p>

  <p>
    We take these seriously and will remove genuinely infringing material
    promptly.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>

  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top changes when we do.
    Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the revised
    version.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about these terms:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a>, or the{" "}
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
